window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-007", "name_zh": "外我", "name_en": "outer ego", "tagline": "你平常以为「是我」的那个自己，只是全我朝外的一张脸：它天生为操纵物质世界而生，背后一直有更大的内我撑着它。", "explanation": "「外我」是你平常以为「是我」的那个自己：完全有意识、朝向物质世界，天生为应付伪装（物质）世界而建构，负责操纵、生存和表面实相。赛斯不是说它不重要，而是说我们太高估了它——它只是全我朝外的一张脸，意识的中心由内我选出，戏是内我写的，外我全然投入地演。它被挡在内在资料之外也是设计：完整的大开大合经验会震垮它，所以潜意识做缓冲、只送最低的量。健康的使用方式不是消灭它，而是平衡与开放的沟通：外我自信而安定，把物质世界的经验传回内我，也允许直觉泉源涌上来。两个自我融合时，一种新意识会出现。它也不是用完就丢的工具：存在之后仍能继续成长，有的外我最终甚至选择成为自己的存有。", "definitions": [{"zh": "“外在自我”与内在自我一同运作，其一，让你能在你所知的世界里操纵自如，另一，带给你那些微妙的内在知觉，没有它们，肉体生活即不可能维持。", "en": "The “outer ego” and the inner ego operate together, the one to enable you to manipulate in the world that you know, the other to bring you those delicate inner perceptions without which physical existence could not be maintained.", "source": "Session 512"}, {"zh": "我不是要低估外在自我，只是你们太高估了它。它真正的本质也没被体认。", "en": "I do not mean to underestimate the outer ego. You have simply overestimated it. Nor has its true nature been recognized.", "source": "Session 512"}, {"zh": "这并不是说外我是个提线木偶。这只是说：外我的意识远少于内自我、少于内我；它的感知较少；它也远不那么稳定——尽管它煞有介事地假装稳定；它是从内我涌出的，它的觉知是更少，而不是更多。（停顿。）", "en": "This is not to say that the outer ego is a puppet. It is to say that the outer ego is far less conscious than the inner ego or the inner self, that its perception is less, that it is far less stable, though it makes great pretense at stability; that it springs from the inner self, and is less rather than more, aware. (Pause.)", "source": "Session 509"}, {"zh": "至于你们那些想知道我将心理学家所谓的潜意识放在哪里的人，你可以想象它是在外在自我与内在自我之间的一个所谓会合之地。", "en": "For those of you who wonder where I place the subconscious, as psychologists think of it, you can imagine it as a meeting place, so to speak, between the outer and inner egos.", "source": "Session 512"}, {"zh": "内在与外在自我并没有一个水泥似的固定关系，但却能以几乎无限的方式彼此关联，而仍保有具体经验的实相，却借主观生活的内在领域给具体实相加上各种不同的颜色。甚至看似未修饰的历史事实，也会因为它们无可避免的浸润其中的象征内容，而被非常不同的经验到。以你们的说法，一次战争真的可以被体验为一个惨烈的灾难、一次人类蛮性的胜利——或被当作人类精神克胜邪恶的崇高胜利。", "en": "The inner and outer egos do not have a cementlike relationship, but can interrelate with each other in almost infinite fashions, still preserving the reality of physical experience, but varying the accents put upon it by the inner areas of subjective life. Even the bare-seeming facts of history are experienced far differently according to the symbolic content within which they are inevitably immersed. A war, in your terms, can be practically experienced as a murderous disaster, a triumph of savagery—or as a sublime victory of the human spirit over evil.", "source": "Session 901"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "外我是什么？你平常以为「是我」的那个自己", "note": "AI总结：外我（外在自我）就是你现在读这句话时觉得「这是我」的那个部分。赛斯开宗明义：不是要低估它，而是你们太高估了它，它真正的本质没被体认。你的更深的本体形成了内我和外我两者、决定你生存在此时此地——外我并不是老板。它被建构来应付伪装（物质）世界：它必须把大部分能量集中在伪装世界的生存和操纵上，因此觉察到的非常少，注意力也被不可避免地收窄。它操纵物质实相，处理的是「次要实相」；内我处理的是首要实相。但它也不是提线木偶：只是它的意识远少于内我，感知较少，也远不那么稳定——尽管它煞有介事地假装稳定。它并不能持续地觉知任何东西，时常忘掉自己；被强烈情绪卷走时似乎失去自己，那时有合一却没有分立感。而它那个「发号施令」的地位，其实完全靠内心层面毫不怀疑地喂养它才维持得住。", "src": "第 35、37、208、509、512、526 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 35 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 37 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 208 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 509 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 512 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 526 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-007-e0001", "zh": "其实，全我一直不断经验所有内在感官传来的资料。内在自我当然觉察到这一点。潜意识有时觉察到这一点，而外在自我觉察到的非常少。其中的原因，我在过去的课程已经解释过了。外在自我必须将其大部分能量集中用于生存和操控外在的伪装世界。这个世界是由内我创造的，它的持续存在则是由于内我持续不断的警觉决定。", "en": "The fact is that the whole self is constantly experiencing data from all of the inner senses. The inner ego is of course aware of this. The subconscious is sometimes aware of this, and the outer ego is aware of very little. I have explained the reasons for this in past sessions. The outer ego must concentrate much of its energy toward survival in and manipulation of the outer camouflage world. This world has already been created by the inner self, and its continuing existence is determined by the constant vigilance of the inner self.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第35节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "35", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0017", "zh": "你们的外在自我，被建构来让你们可以应对伪装世界。这是必要的。可是它也不可避免地，缩窄了你们的关注范围和理解程度。在你们的存在期间，外在自我让你们聚焦、长在、放在、专注你们的物质宇宙上。它处理你们对伪装物质的操纵。", "en": "Your outside egos are constructed to enable you to deal with the camouflage world. It is necessary. It necessarily also narrows your concentration and your understanding. During your existence you are focused, you are stuck to, you are placed and centered in, your physical universe by the outside ego. It manages your manipulation of camouflage material.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第37节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "37", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0088", "zh": "因此如你们所知，我们区分一个外在自我，它操纵着物质实相，和一个内在自我，它指挥着内我的活动。那么现在，下一步就应该很清楚了。基本上，自我处理次要实相，而内在自我处理首要实相。", "en": "As you know therefore we have differentiated between an outer ego, who manipulates within physical reality, and an inner ego who directs the activities of the inner self. Now then, the next step should indeed be clear. In the main, the ego deals with secondary realities, and in the main, the inner ego deals with primaries.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第208节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "208", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0102", "zh": "这并不是说外我是个提线木偶。这只是说：外我的意识远少于内自我、少于内我；它的感知较少；它也远不那么稳定——尽管它煞有介事地假装稳定；它是从内我涌出的，它的觉知是更少，而不是更多。（停顿。）", "en": "This is not to say that the outer ego is a puppet. It is to say that the outer ego is far less conscious than the inner ego or the inner self, that its perception is less, that it is far less stable, though it makes great pretense at stability; that it springs from the inner self, and is less rather than more, aware. (Pause.)", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第509节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "509", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0103", "zh": "用你们的话说，外我并不能持续地觉知任何东西。它时常忘掉自己。当它被一种强烈的情绪卷走，它似乎失去了它自己。那时便有合一，却没有分立感；而当它最用力地守住自己的个体感时，它便不再觉知那种合一。", "en": "The outer ego is not continuously, in your terms, aware of anything. It frequently forgets itself. When it becomes swept up in a strong emotion it seems to lose itself. There is unity then but no sense of apartness. When it most vigorously maintains its sense of individuality it is no longer aware of unity-with.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第509节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "509", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0105", "zh": "但是你还有一个部分，你更深的本体，它形成“内我”与“外我”，它决定你生存在此时此地。“这”就是你本体的核心，你从中跃出的“心灵种子”，你为其一部分的“多次元人格”。", "en": "There is however a portion of you, the deeper identity who forms both the inner ego and the outer ego, who decided that you would be a physical being in this place and in this time. This is the core of your identity, the psychic seed from which you sprang, the multidimensional personality of which you are part.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第512节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "512", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0108", "zh": "我不是要低估外在自我，只是你们太高估了它。它真正的本质也没被体认。", "en": "I do not mean to underestimate the outer ego. You have simply overestimated it. Nor has its true nature been recognized.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第512节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "512", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0110", "zh": "通往心理及心灵的通道永远存在，讯息在多重“我”的层次中被来回的传递着。“自我”毫不犹豫的接受由内我传来有用的消息与资料，事实上它的地位仰仗的都是这种对内在资料毫不怀疑就接受的态度。“自我”换句话说即是你的“外我”，它之所以能保持它自己的安全及它那看起来好像在发号施令的地位，完全由于你们自己的内心层面允许它这么做的原故。内心层面也同时维持了肉体的运作，并与外来的以及内在的众多刺激保持沟通。各种或然世界的生存经验以及转世的经历并不会使灵魂或全我萎缩，反而是向外扩大。有关“或然世界”我以后再解释。", "en": "Channels, psychological and psychic, always exist, sending communications back and forth through the various levels of the self, and the ego accepts necessary information and data from inner portions of the personality without question. Its position in fact depends in a large manner upon this unquestioning acceptance of inner data. The ego, in other words, the “exterior” self that you think of as your self — that portion of you maintains its safety and its seeming command precisely because inner layers of your own personality constantly uphold it, keep the physical body operating, and maintain communications with the multitudinous stimuli that come both from outside conditions and inside conditions. The soul or entity is not diminished but expanded through reincarnations, through existence and experience in probable realities — something that I will explain later.", "source": "时空之外 · 第526节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "526", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "外我的本职：伪装世界的操盘手", "note": "AI总结：外我有一份正经工作，而且做得不坏。它是全我里被派去维持物质操纵的那个部分，只透过肉体装备、只透过外在感官感知；它像 surfaces 的专家——人类主要依赖外我的种种力量，而它的目的就是跟表面实相打交道。这不是说表面实相不重要，只是这样得到的资讯有限，其他力量由潜意识去处理和平衡。对伪装材料的操控，很大程度上取决于外我的自信，而这份自信只有当它追随内我的模式时才会强大。赛斯还给了两个传神的比方：外我是自己那往外看的表面，像个坐在房子前廊、丢着内在工作不管的照顾者；它又是全我里被允许完全迷醉于自我催眠出神的那一小部分。它嫉妒自己的位置，受不了有任何事情藏着，可它自身行为的机制恰恰对它自己隐藏——它只知道自己的表面感觉。它也有义务不只表达自己，还要（程度较小地）表达构成潜意识的那些隐藏人格。赛斯甚至说物质外形是实相采取的一种「伪装」——伪装是真的，但它里面还有大得多的实相。", "src": "第 37、99、119、120、512 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 37 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 99 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 119 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 120 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 512 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-007-e0019", "zh": "对伪装材料的操控，在很大程度上取决于外在自我的自信，而外在自我的自信，只有当它追随内在自我的模式时，力量才会强大。你可以暂时假装不相信这种必要的信仰，但是你的销售能力的根基是，你有自信可以当个整合又有原则的人格。实际上来讲，你会发现你的能力降到最低的程度，你还跟我谈实用性吗？", "en": "The manipulation of camouflage material depends to a large degree upon the outside ego’s confidence, and the outside ego's confidence is only strong when it follows the inner ego’s pattern. You can for a while fake the sort of disbelieving belief required, but your ability to sell is based upon your own confidence as an integrated and principled personality. Practically you would find your ability minimized, and do you speak to me about practicality?", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第37节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "37", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0055", "zh": "但如你所知的外在自我就是全我致力于维持物质操纵的那个部分，它只透过那些物质设备感知那些外在感官。它看到它的领土危在旦夕而严阵以待。它，自我，就是全我的那个小小的部分，全我允许它完全，或几乎完全，迷醉在自我催眠的出神之中。它就是暗中相信催眠师特定说明的那个部分，因此它将是最后离开这种出神的一个部分。", "en": "But the outer ego as you know is that portion of the whole self that is given over to the maintenance of physical manipulations, and it perceives only through those physical equipment, those outer senses. It sees its dominion in jeopardy and rises up in arms. It, the ego, is that small portion of the whole self which the whole self has allowed to be completely, or almost completely, bewitched by the self-hypnotic trance. It is that portion which believes implicitly in the given specifications of the hypnotist, and as such it will be last to leave the trance.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第99节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "99", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0060", "zh": "后来发展出来的外在自我。嫉妒它的位置，想要一手掌握所有的知识。这是不可能的。它受不了把任何事情藏起来，但它自身行为的机制却正好就藏起来不让自己知道，所以它只知道自己表面的感觉而已。", "en": "The outer ego, being of later development, is jealous of its position and would have all knowledge at its fingertips. This is impossible. It cannot stand to have anything hidden, but the very mechanism of its own behavior is hidden from itself, and it knows only the feel of its own surfaces.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第119节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "119", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0061", "zh": "在很多方面，它是一个反映者，自己那往外看的表面。虽然这是必要的，但自己整个剩下来的部分不能留给一个没有把注意力集中在深处之内，而是坐在房子的前廊，丢着内在工作不管的组织者或照顾者。外在自我不想要见到内在自我。外在自我不想要承认内在自我的存在。就像没有镜子，眼睛看不到它自己的瞳孔，同样的，要不是内在自我藏在所有倒影的深处，外在自我连它自己都看不到。", "en": "In many respects it is a reflector, the surface of the self looking outward. While this is necessary, the whole remainder of the self could not be left to an organizer or caretaker who did not focus his attentions within the depths but sat, as it were, on the front porch of the house, leaving the inner workings unattended. The outer ego does not want to meet the inner ego. The outer ego does not want to admit the existence of the inner ego. As the eye cannot see its own pupil without a mirror, so the outer ego could not even see itself, were it not that the inner ego hides in the depths of all reflections.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第119节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "119", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0066", "zh": "这个外在自我，它的目的之一，是有义务不只表达它自己，也要表达构成潜意识的那些隐藏的不同人格，但程度较小。就更大、更广泛的角度而言，全我，整体潜意识和内我的全部场域，往回延伸到存有。任何一个自己的前世投射或存在，是没有终点的；但是在你们的场域里却不被了解，任何一个自己的潜意识那向前的冲刺是没有终点的。", "en": "This out ego, among its purposes, has the duty of expressing not only itself but to a lesser extent those various hidden personalities which compose the subconscious. In larger terms and in more comprehensive terms, the whole self, the whole field of the complete subconscious and inner self, reaches back to the entity. There is no end to the past projection or existence of the subconscious of any given self; and though it is not understood in your field, there is no end to the forward thrust of the subconscious of any given self.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第119节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "119", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0067", "zh": "不同种类的力量也被这些场域运用在你们的宇宙上。在彻底了解它之前，不可能产生真正的进步。人类依然和表面打交道，像他现在这样主要依赖外在自我的种种力量，而它的目的是和表面实相打交道。", "en": "Force of various kinds is also exerted by these fields upon your universe. Until it is thoroughly understood little real progress can be made. Mankind still deals with surfaces, depending mainly as he does upon the powers of the outer ego, whose purpose it is to deal only with surface reality.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第120节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "120", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0068", "zh": "这并不是说，这样的表面实相无关紧要，或某些关于它自身本质的资讯无法从它的研究中拾得；而是说，这样只能得到少量资讯。我谈过的其他场域在现存的物质有机体身上发挥它们的影响力。处理和平衡这些力量的是潜意识，不是外在自我。", "en": "This is not to say that such surface reality is not vital and important, or that some information about its own nature cannot be gleaned from its study; but only a small amount can be so obtained. The other fields of which I speak exert their influences upon the physical organism as it exists. These forces are dealt with and balanced by the subconscious, and not by the outer ego.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第120节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "120", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0109", "zh": "且说有时我会用到“伪装”这个名词，指的是外在自我所涉及的物质世界，因为物质外形是实相所采取的一种伪装。这伪装是真的，但在它内还有一个大得多的实相——一个赋予它形式的活力。然后你的肉体感官让你去感知这伪装，因为感官以极为专门化的方式与之配合。但要想感觉到那内在形式的实相，则需要另一类的注意力及更精微的操纵，这不是肉体感官所能胜任的。", "en": "Now at times I will be using the term “camouflage,” referring to the physical world to which the outer ego relates, for physical form is one of the camouflages that reality adopts. The camouflage is real, and yet there is a much greater reality within it — the vitality that gave it form. Your physical senses then allow you to perceive this camouflage, for they are attuned to it in a highly specialized manner. But to sense the reality within the form requires a different sort of attention, and more delicate manipulations than the physical senses provide.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第512节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "512", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "为什么外我被挡在内在资料之外？", "note": "AI总结：外我接触不到内在讯息，不是意外，而是设计。它生来就是跟伪装模式打交道的，整组内在感官带来的了悟会把它震得没法承受——连直接内在经验的稀释版本对它都是震撼，因为它把自己和自己的知觉想象成至高无上。于是潜意识充当缓冲：筛掉大部分内在资料，只把最低的量送给外我。内在自我则在觉知着一切——它在危险警告外我之前就已觉察，它熟悉外我一无所知的活动和方法。这种屏蔽甚至延伸到时间：内在自我不受连续时刻的束缚，外我则被迫进入一个接一个的行动里。最妙的是，内在资料其实一直被人类架构的每一个其他部分自动接受——唯独外我不收；可它又常在毫不知情的状况下靠着这些它不承认收到的资讯行动，还往往因此逃过灾祸。往深处看，外我在某种程度上本该代表仍然住在潜意识里的那些「第二支配人格」；当它太狭隘、代表不好时，它们就会揭竿而起，趁它软弱时表达自己。而外我的观点天生被自己的企图限制：它企图把行动截短，只感知得到它的出生和死亡，出生之前、死亡之后都看不见。", "src": "第 35、36、38、42、119、120、290 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 35 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 36 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 38 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 42 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 119 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 120 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 290 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-007-e0002", "zh": "只有建立某种程度的信心，外在自我才有余力熟悉这些内在运作，至少在你们的层面是如此。否则，你们就会犹豫不前。原则上来说，即使全我有能力组织所有来自内在感官的资料，潜意识也很少能完完全全接收这样的讯息；而外在自我关注的是伪装模式，而且也的确是天生与伪装模式打交道，所以对整组内在感官带来的了悟，震撼得简直没办法法承受。", "en": "Only when a certain level of confidence is reached can the outer ego afford to become familiar with these inner workings, at least on your plane. Otherwise you would falter. As a rule, even though the whole self is capable of organizing the data from all of the inner senses, the subconscious can rarely receive such communications full blast; and the outer ego, concerned as it is with camouflage pattern, and really born to deal with camouflage pattern, simply could not stand the shock of realization that a complete set of inner senses would bring.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第35节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "35", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0003", "zh": "外在自我无可避免总是会避开这类经验。在你们的层面，即使是一种直接内在经验的稀释版本，对外在自我而言都是一种震撼，因为自我把自己及其知觉想像成是至高无上的。你们连对你们有什么训练，都毫无概念，对这样的完整经验让外在自我有多震撼，更是如此。所以我们一次取得一种内在感官的经验就好了。", "en": "This sort of experience will always be shielded from the outer ego of necessity. Even a watered-down version of a direct inner experience is a shock to the outer ego on your plane, since the ego imagines itself and its own perceptions to be supreme. You have no idea, even with what training you have, of how shattering such a complete experience would be to the outer ego, so we will take one inner-sense experience at a time.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第35节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "35", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0006", "zh": "潜意识——来继续完成我已经开始的内容——潜意识，的确会缓冲真正实相对外在自我的冲击。如果对你们而言，有时候仿佛活在一个梦世界里，那在很多方面，你们是这样没错。你们的力量还不足以承受基本实相的冲击，所以你们建构复杂的梦世界，以便找到避难处，躲开你们看起来野蛮、失控又没章法的混乱。", "en": "The subconscious—to finish what I began—the subconscious cushions the outer ego really against the shock of true reality. If sometimes it seems to you that you are living in a dream world, in many respects you are. You are not strong enough yet to bear the brunt of basic reality, and you construct complicated dream worlds in order to find shelter from what would appear to you as savage, uncontrolled and undisciplined chaos.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第35节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "35", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0008", "zh": "就像极快乐或极痛苦的强烈经验往往会掩盖其他事情一样，实相的直接经验也会，但是只会完全地掩盖直接经验它的外在自我。在你们的层次上，潜意识的过滤是需要的，而这也是鲁柏在上课时要解离的主要原因之一，即便他的内在实相经验，可以说是透过我而取得二手经验也一样。", "en": "As the intense experience of great joy or pain often blots out everything else, so would the direct experience of reality blot out, only completely, the outer ego who experienced it directly. At your level the sieve of the subconscious is a necessity and that is one of the main reasons why Ruburt dissociates during our sessions, even though his experience of inner reality is received second handed, so to speak, through me.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第35节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "35", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0011", "zh": "你们知道，你们的钟表时间是伪装，对内在自我而言，钟表时间并不存在。这一点你们的确不应该觉得奇怪，因为你们知道，你们现在的人格甚至可以通过使用心理时间，而在一定程度上逃离钟表时间。我曾经说过，没有障碍，就没有时间。内在自我意识到的障碍很少，因此被时间束缚的程度不像外在自我那么大。", "en": "Your clock time as you know is camouflage, and does not exist as far as the inner ego is concerned. This certainly should not be strange to you, since you know that even your present personalities can to some extent escape from clock time through the use of psychological time. I have said that there is no time without barriers. The inner ego is aware of fewer barriers and therefore is not bound by time to the degree that the outer ego is bound.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第36节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "36", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0020", "zh": "这个内在感官像所有其他内在感官一样，正被内在自我意识自我使用，但是外在自我在这方面未被允许可以知道。所以来自这些内在感官的资料，经过潜意识筛选过滤之后，送给外在自我，数量已经是低得无法再低，也就是最低的量了。", "en": "Now this sense, like all other inner senses, is being used by the inner self-conscious ego, but the outer ego is not permitted awareness along these lines. A minimum amount of information from these inner senses is given to the outer ego after it is sifted through the subconscious. But only a minimum amount.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第38节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "38", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0024", "zh": "这是发生了什么。当意识自我渴望讯息，而外在自我也完全在控制当中时，这个讯息就会从外在感官来搜寻。当外在自我不知不觉是被箝制住，而这个讯息也被需要的时候，潜意识就会透过内在感官的使用来传送这个讯息。你们将会知道，事实就是如此。", "en": "What happened was this. When the conscious ego desires information, and when the outer ego is in full control, then the information is sought from the outer senses. When the outer ego is caught unawares and information is requested, the subconscious often delivers it through the use of the inner senses. You will see that this was the case.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第42节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "42", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0057", "zh": "在潜意识所有个人化的面向背后是自我或者说指挥意识；（directive consciousness）；不过是以休眠的方式，而且和荣格的论点相反的是，在潜意识之内以及在它那些个人化的面向之中，会发现过去转世的自己残余的记忆人格。它们可以被称为阴影，但它们并不是没有力量的。内在自我，潜意识的组织指挥者，也是自己的一部分，熟悉外在自我一无所知的活动和方法。这个组织者不仅从里面指挥肉体的活动，也从外面指挥那些个人的存活机制，没有那些机制，肉体无法存在，而且外在自我的存在也非常依赖它们。", "en": "It is the ego or directive consciousness behind all personified aspects of the subconscious; in dormant fashion however, and contrary to Jung’s propositions, within the subconscious and in those personified aspects of it will be found remnant memory personalities of past reincarnated selves. They may be called shadows and yet they are not powerless. The inner ego, the directive organizer of the subconscious, also is the part of the self which is familiar with activities and methods of which the outer ego is ignorant. It is this organizer who directs not only the movements of the physical body from within, but directs from within those intimate survival mechanisms, without which the physical body could not exist, and upon which the existence of the outer ego is so dependent.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第119节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "119", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0064", "zh": "内在自我知道何时运用安全阀，也会在外在自我注意到之前觉察到危险。内在自我和维护全我的基础与平衡有关，这非常重要，而乐于听取来自整体存有的讯息。内在自我透过内在感官接收讯息，对于外在自我因为它的专门化而无能认出的种种实相是有觉察的。在某些重要的面向上，外在自我本来某种程度代表依然居住在潜意识里的第二支配人格（subdominant personalities）。当外在自我狭隘，不足以代表这些第二支配人格时，它们就会揭竿而起，并趁状况有利之际，企图透过支配自我那一边暂时的软弱，来表达它们自己。但即使不这样做，它们也可以趁外在自我有幸浑然不觉时暂时接管，或透过单一功能，像是说话或动作，来表达它们自己。", "en": "The inner ego knows when to apply safety valves, and is aware of the danger before the outer ego is alerted. The inner ego is concerned with maintaining the foundations and balance, which is very important, of the whole self, and it is open to messages from the overall entity. The inner ego receives messages through the inner senses, and is aware of realities which the outer ego cannot afford to recognize because of its specialization. In some important aspects the outer ego is supposed to represent to some degree the subdominant personalities who still dwell in the subconscious. When the outer ego is narrow, and poorly represents these subdominant personalities then they rise up in arms, and when conditions are favorable attempt to express themselves through a momentary weakness on the part of the dominant ego. But without even doing this they may momentarily take over or express themselves through a single function, such as speech or motion, while the outer ego is blissfully unaware.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第119节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "119", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0069", "zh": "千里眼是存在而且是可能的，因为它的基础在广阔的现在之内，这之所以不为人知，是因为人类不会接受可得的资料。千里眼存在，因为物质和能量是同一件事。在肉体本身的器官之内有千里眼，因为身体的器官不“只是”物质，而是能量把它自己组成物质。这样的内在资料持续而且自动被人类架构的每一个其他部分接受，除了外在自我以外。甚至这个外在自我，话说回来，也在毫不知情的状况下，经常根据它不承认它接收到的这类资讯而行动；而且这样的行动往往把它从悲惨状况中解救出来。", "en": "Clairvoyance exists and is possible because of its basis within the spacious present, and this is not known because man will not accept the available data. Clairvoyance exists because matter and energy are one and the same thing. There is clairvoyance within the organs of the physical body itself, because the organs of the body are not, quote, “just” matter, but energy which has composed itself into matter. Such inner data continually and automatically is accepted by every other portion of the human framework except by the outer ego. Even this outer ego, however, acts all unknowingly often on the basis of such information, which it will not admit it has received; and often such action saves it from dire circumstances.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第120节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "120", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0097", "zh": "内在自我看见也知道它自己是这个行动或事件的一部分，而且它看见整个本体同时存在于各个不同的维度之中。外在自我企图缩短行动，所以它的观点受到它自己的企图限制。它感知它的出生和它的死亡，却没有超越它的出生和它的死亡。", "en": "The inner ego sees and knows itself as a part of this action or happening, and sees the entire identity existing in various dimensions simultaneously. The outer ego attempts to cut action short, and so its viewpoint is limited by its own attempt. It perceives its birth and its death, but not beyond its birth or its death.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第290节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "290", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "台前幕后：内我写的戏，外我演出的角色", "note": "AI总结：外我和内我的分工，赛斯讲得非常清楚：内我是荣格会叫作「无意识」的那些经验的组织者——外我在物质实相里操纵，内我在内在实相里组织与操纵；是内我创造出那重物理实相，外我随后才与之打交道。内我由自身、由它的组分与内在经验，丰饶地塑出一个物质对应物，好让外我在其中演出自己的角色——外我全然投入角色，演着一出内我所写的戏。两边不是主仆，更像两张脸：内在自我向内聚焦、朝着发端的冲动回溯，外我往外冲刺；潜意识可以被想成一个被两者包围的核心。情感在你们这一端变化、转化，变成连结外我和内我的内在感官连结物；分子意识保留本体形成的完形意识就是自我、外我，再被内我的意识利用。定位上：潜意识是外我与内我之间的一个会合之地，而自己并没有真实的分界。连细胞意识都可以粗略地说：细胞意识之于内我，如同潜意识之于外我。全我则大于各部分的总和——内我指引所有高度主观的活动，外我在物质环境中负责自己。", "src": "第 45、49、55、58、177、290、509、512 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 45 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 49 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 55 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 58 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 177 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 290 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 509 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 512 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-007-e0025", "zh": "在潜意识的上层区域，只有相对来说一小层个人资料，因此是自我本位的扭曲资料。一般来说，这一层很快就能被认出来。鲁柏现在就可以把它认出来，而他既不是科学家，也不是心理学家。声明一下，你了解我说的自我本位资料，指的是和外在伪装导向的人格有关的部分，而且更强大的内在自我实际上代表外在自我背后的力量与能力。", "en": "There is only a relatively small layer of personal material, and therefore egotistical and distortive material, at the upper reaches of the subconscious. This layer can be quickly recognized, as a rule. Ruburt recognizes it now, and he is no scientist or psychologist. For the record, you understand that I am referring to egotistical material as that portion that is concerned with the outer camouflage- oriented personality, and that the stronger inner ego actually represents the power and ability behind the outer ego.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第45节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "45", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0026", "zh": "我已经跟你解释过，内我是如何地连接到当前人格，以及，情感是如何在你们这一端通过潜意识层而变化，在你们层面开始作为人格的一部分，作为你力场（force field）的一部分，然后被转化，变为内在感知（inner-sense）的连结物，连结外在自我和内我。", "en": "I have explained to you how the inner self is connected to the present personality, and how the emotions at your end change through the layers of the subconscious, begin in your plane as parts of the personality, and as part of your force field, and then are transformed and become the innersense connective that connects the outer ego to the inner self.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第49节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "49", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0031", "zh": "这结合的分子意识，保留本体，形成一个完形意识，就是自我、外在自我，接着再被内在自我的意识利用。内在自我不受你们层面的法则牵制，只要它在物质的诞生时进入你们的层面，就能离开肉体，再重建它。", "en": "The combined molecular consciousnesses, retaining identity, form a gestalt consciousness that is the ego, the outer ego, that is in turn utilized by the consciousness of the inner ego. The inner ego being unhampered by the laws of your plane, once having entered your plane at physical birth, can therefore leave the physical body and then reconstruct it.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第55节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "55", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0033", "zh": "就自己与非自己来说，你们知道，自己这个单位是由主导整个能量场的内在自我组织起来的。外在自我指挥这个完形在物质宇宙中的操纵。外在自我与物质属性的关系更紧密，而且它能够透过调整自己配合内我而改变焦点，用内在而非外在感官来聚焦能量，而直接体验内在实相。这是目前为止最有利的内在实相体验方法，因为外在自我因此能够有意识地觉察事情的来龙去脉，也能够在它自己的范畴中利用这种知识。", "en": "As far as self and not-self are concerned, the unit of self is organized, as you know, by the inner ego, which directs the whole energy field. The outer ego directs the manipulation of this gestalt in the physical universe. The outer ego is rather more tied to physical properties, and yet it can directly experience inner reality by a change of focus through aligning itself with the inner ego, focusing its energies with the inner rather than the outer senses. This is by far the most advantageous method of experiencing inner reality, because the outer ego is therefore consciously aware of what has been going on, and can use such knowledge in its own sphere.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0084", "zh": "内在自我会指引所有高度主观的活动。而外在自我，如你们所知，会在物质环境中负责自己。你们必须记得，全我大于各部分的总合；而且，由于全我就是行动，所以它时时刻刻都不一样。因此不管什么时候，要精确定位人格是不可能的。全我不只是你们在你们时间内所认识的人格之总和，也是它曾经所是与未来所是的总和。因为就如我之前的解释，行动具有同时性，而时间正如你们所以为的，是由你们自己的身体知觉所形成。", "en": "The inner ego directs all activities which are deeply subjective. The outer ego as you know deals with the manipulation of the self in the physical environment. You must remember that the whole self is more than the sum of its parts; and also, since it is action, it is never the same. It is therefore impossible at any moment to pinpoint the personality. Therefore the whole self is not only the sum of the personality as you know it in your time, it is also the sum of what it has been and what it shall be. For as I have explained action is simultaneous, and time as you think of it is caused by your own physical perception.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第177节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "177", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0098", "zh": "细胞意识是内在自我或内我的一部分。从非常宽松的角度来说，细胞意识之于内我，正如同潜意识之于外在自我。不管怎样，当然有很多差异。", "en": "Cellular consciousness is a part of the consciousness of the inner ego or inner self. Very loosely speaking, cellular consciousness is to the inner self what the subconscious is to the outer ego. There are of course many differences however.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第290节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "290", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0100", "zh": "内自我正是那些荣格会称为无意识的经验的组织者。内自我是我们所称的内我的另一个名称。外我在环境与物理实相之中操纵运作，内自我、或者说内我，便在内在的实相之中组织与操纵。内自我创造出那重物理实相，外我随后才与之打交道。", "en": "Now the inner ego is the organizer of experience that Jung would call unconscious. The inner ego is another term for what we call the inner self. As the outer ego manipulates within the environment and physical reality, so the inner ego or self organizes and manipulates within an inner reality. The inner ego creates that physical reality with which the outer ego then deals.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第509节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "509", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0101", "zh": "这内我的能量，由它自己导引、运用，从它自身、从它的组分与内在经验中，丰饶地塑出一个物质的对应物，好让外我在其中演出自己的角色。外我全然投入角色，演着一出内我所写的戏。", "en": "The energy of this inner self is directed and used by it to richly form from itself, from components and inner experience, a material counterpart in which the outer ego then can act out its role. The outer ego is most in the role, acting out a play that the inner self has written.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第509节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "509", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0104", "zh": "“外在自我”与内在自我一同运作，其一，让你能在你所知的世界里操纵自如，另一，带给你那些微妙的内在知觉，没有它们，肉体生活即不可能维持。", "en": "The “outer ego” and the inner ego operate together, the one to enable you to manipulate in the world that you know, the other to bring you those delicate inner perceptions without which physical existence could not be maintained.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第512节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "512", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0106", "zh": "至于你们那些想知道我将心理学家所谓的潜意识放在哪里的人，你可以想象它是在外在自我与内在自我之间的一个所谓会合之地。不过你必须了解，自己并没有真实的分界，因此我们说到各个不同的部分只是为阐明基本的概念而已。", "en": "For those of you who wonder where I place the subconscious, as psychologists think of it, you can imagine it as a meeting place, so to speak, between the outer and inner egos. You must understand that there are no real divisions to the self, however, so we speak of various portions only to make the basic idea clear.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第512节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "512", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "外我用对了是什么样：平衡、健康、顺流", "note": "AI总结：赛斯反复强调的不是消灭外我，而是平衡。当内我和外我追求完全相反的观点和目标时，困难就来了——一道近乎全面的障碍立在两者之间，全我在很大程度上就被拒于价值完成之外。反过来说，当两者平衡、有讯息交流，内我能直接与外我沟通、带给它必要的启蒙，让它分享内我那浓缩的理解；外我也能把物质世界的经验传回给内我，实际帮内我扩展——内我显然需要具备外在感官的外我，才能在各个伪装形式中具体化、增益自己的价值完成。健康的事也一样：维护身体功能、负责身体健康的是那个内在指挥者，健康不佳时你该沟通的对象是它；你甚至可能不知不觉得病又痊愈，因为内我知道病与痊愈的理由，在架构二里安排了补救的情境。日常版更简单：想写一封信你就会去做——欲望、信念和实行之间没有冲突，行动顺畅流出；一旦你相信这件事危险，创造的流就被你自己堵住了。所以内在与外在自我之间的沟通，显然应该尽可能清晰而开放。这个关系也不是水泥做的：内外自我能以几乎无限的方式彼此关联，同一场战争可以被体验成惨烈的灾难，也可以被体验成人类精神的崇高胜利。", "src": "第 58、119、120、822、901 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 58 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 119 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 120 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 822 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 901 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-007-e0034", "zh": "当内在自我与外在自我追求完全相反的观点以及不同的目标和目的时，你们就遇到困难了。在研究人类的人格和心灵上，你们的心理学家走得不远，也不够深。当一道全面，或接近全面的障碍存在内在自我与外在自我之间时，全我就会很大程度被拒于价值完成之外。这样的分割曾在历史上发生过好几次，目前也正在发生。", "en": "When the inner ego and the outer ego pursue directly opposed viewpoints and different aims and goals, then you run into difficulty. In studying human personality and the psyche, your psychologists have not gone far, nor deeply enough. When a complete barrier, or nearly complete barrier, exists between the inner and outer egos, then the whole self is denied value fulfillment to a large degree. Such a division occurs at various times in history, and is occurring now.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0035", "zh": "当这两者在一种平衡状态时，当它们之间有讯息交流时，内在自我就能直接与外在自我沟通，并带给它必要的启蒙，也使它，也就是使外在自我从它自己，内在自我自己，拥有的浓缩理解，以及直接参与整体宇宙的存在获益。", "en": "When the two are in balance and when there is communication between them, then the inner ego can directly communicate with the outer ego, bring to it the necessary enlightenments, and give it, that is give the outer ego the benefit of its own, the inner ego’s own, condensed comprehension and direct participation in the existence of the universe as a whole.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0036", "zh": "外在自我在这样有利的状况下，也比较几乎有能力把它在物质世界的经验传达给内我，从而实际帮助内我的扩展，然后内我得以直接体验它在伪装模式中唯有如此才体验得到的刺激和操纵。", "en": "The outer ego, under such advantageous circumstances, is more nearly able also to communicate its experience in the physical world to the inner self, and hereby to actually help enlarge the inner self, which then directly experiences stimulation and manipulations in a camouflage pattern which is otherwise denied to it.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0037", "zh": "内我显然需要具备外在感官的外在自我，才能允许它本身在各个不同伪装形式中的具体化。这不应该被低估或遗忘。没有这外在核心，内我根本无法透过参与能量-建构（energy-constructs加连字符）增益它自己的价值完成。", "en": "The inner self obviously needs the outer ego with its outer senses, in order to permit its own materialization in various camouflage forms. This should not be underrated or forgotten. Without the outer core, the inner self could simply not add to its own value fulfillment through participation in energy-constructs （hyphen）.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0058", "zh": "这些功能全部都是由这个内在指挥者在维护，身体的健康也是由它负责。当你的健康不佳时，你必须沟通的对象就是这个指挥者。做这件事有许多方法，改天我们会讨论。以它们对潜意识每一层或每一区都有意义的这样一种方式，选择梦象征的就是这个内在指挥者，透过直接给外在自我的潜意识资料数量、速度和类型也是由它负责。", "en": "It is this inner director who maintains all of these functions, and who is responsible for the physical health. It is this director to whom you must communicate when health fails. There are ways of doing this which we will discuss at later date. It is this inner director who chooses the dream symbols in such a way that they will be meaningful to all layers or areas of the subconscious, and who is responsible for the amount, rate and type of subconscious data which is given to the outer ego by means of the intuitions.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第119节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "119", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0059", "zh": "如果外在自我对于在平等的基础上，和它的内在对等物合作感到满足，就可以避开很多严重的问题了。", "en": "If the outer ego would be content to work on an equal basis with its inner counterpart, then many severe difficulties would be sidestepped.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第119节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "119", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0070", "zh": "两个主要的可能性来到脑海里。一个是，由于自我失去控制，持续缺少内我的接受，可能导致全世界的灾难。第二个是，被束缚和否定太久的内我，可能大爆发让自我无法招架，以至于在物质场域的存在变得非常困难，因为自我的配备是用来处理这种操纵的。自我的支配确实必须停止，但是一定要以外我和内我之间的平衡取而代之。今晚简短提到的其他事情，以后也会更彻底地讨论。", "en": "Two main possibilities come to mind. One, a continued lack of acceptance of the inner self could lead to worldwide catastrophe, as the ego runs wild. Two, the inner self, restrained and denied for too long a period, could explosively overwhelm the ego so that existence in the physical field was made most difficult, since the ego is equipped to handle such manipulation. ego domination must indeed be halted, but it must be replaced with a balance between the outer and inner selves. Other matters briefly mentioned this evening will be more thoroughly discussed then also.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第120节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "120", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0114", "zh": "口授：那么，再一次的，你可能不知不觉的染上一种病又恢复了，却从来没有觉察过你的毛病，而你被治愈是因为一连串似乎与那病本身毫无关系的事件——因为在“架构二”里内我知道患病及其痊愈的理由，带来会弥补那状况的那些适当的情境。当没有事阻碍了复原的时候，这种事情就会自动的发生。 在内在与外在自我之间的沟通显然应该尽可能的清晰而开放。一般而言，内我依靠你对具体事件的估量。你对你生活隐私面的关注以及你在群体事件中的参与，都与你对具体情况的估量以及你对它的信念与欲望极有关系。", "en": "Dictation: You may then, again, unknowingly acquire an illness and recover, never aware of your malady, being healed because of a series of events that would seemingly have nothing to do with the illness itself — because in Framework 2 the inner ego, knowing both the reason for the illness, and its cure, brought about those precise situations that remedied the condition. Such events happen automatically, when nothing hampers recovery at your end.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第822节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "822", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0115", "zh": "举一个非常简单的例子：如果你想写一封信，你就会去做。在你的欲望、信念及那个行为的实行之间没有冲突，因此那个行为本身顺畅的流出。如果为了某个理由，经由一个对你现况差劲的估量，你相信这样子的一件行为是危险的，那么你就会阻碍在欲望与实行之间的那个流出。由内我开始那个创造之流会被阻碍。", "en": "The communication between the inner and outer egos should obviously be as clear and open as possible. As a general rule, the inner ego depends upon your assessment of physical events. Your involvement in the private aspects of your living, and your participation in mass events, has much to do with your estimation of the physical situation, and with your beliefs and desires regarding it. Give us a moment … A very simple example (colon): If you want to write a letter you do so. There is no conflict between your desires, beliefs, and the execution of the act, so the action itself flows smoothly. If for some reason or another, through a poor assessment of your reality, you believe that such an act is dangerous, then you will hamper the flow between the desire and the execution. The flow of creativity begun by the inner ego will be impeded.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第822节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "822", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0116", "zh": "内在与外在自我并没有一个水泥似的固定关系，但却能以几乎无限的方式彼此关联，而仍保有具体经验的实相，却借主观生活的内在领域给具体实相加上各种不同的颜色。甚至看似未修饰的历史事实，也会因为它们无可避免的浸润其中的象征内容，而被非常不同的经验到。以你们的说法，一次战争真的可以被体验为一个惨烈的灾难、一次人类蛮性的胜利——或被当作人类精神克胜邪恶的崇高胜利。", "en": "The inner and outer egos do not have a cementlike relationship, but can interrelate with each other in almost infinite fashions, still preserving the reality of physical experience, but varying the accents put upon it by the inner areas of subjective life. Even the bare-seeming facts of history are experienced far differently according to the symbolic content within which they are inevitably immersed. A war, in your terms, can be practically experienced as a murderous disaster, a triumph of savagery—or as a sublime victory of the human spirit over evil.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第901节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "901", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "心灵探险的先决条件：一个有自信的外我", "note": "AI总结：想探索内在实相，出发点恰恰不是甩掉外我，而是把它安顿好。一个有信心的自我是心灵探险的先决条件——只有有自信的外我，才能最终觉得够安全，敢给内我留出回旋的余地。练习出体（灵体投射）就是典型场景：投射常常在睡眠中发生，醒时也会发生，只是自我通常不觉察；透过训练，内我和外我之间有更多沟通，自我才有机会明白发生了什么。更深的一步是融合：当你带着醒时的「我」进入梦状态，或者那个门户在醒时开启，内在自我和外在自我就会融合——这种融合代表一种新意识的形成。过程通常是这样：外我感应到它平时进不去的实相，想「还有更多，但我无法跟过去」；有了这个了悟，内我可能突然开启，直觉泉源冲到表面，而外我因为已被提醒过，能够接受这些实相、同时照常履行日常职责。它从此不再怕直觉资料、不再抗拒内在感官、不再害怕自己在直觉洪流中的存活。本体不再只限于外我——它变得熟悉全我，取用到以前没觉察的力量。旺盛的精力、格外好的健康、能记得并操纵梦，都是这种新意识出现的征兆。赛斯还举过一个反面例子：约瑟梦里看见自己站在后窗，内外自我融合了，却因为受惊的外我拦了一下，错过了一次绝佳的投射。", "src": "第 90、202、283 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 90 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 202 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 283 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-007-e0053", "zh": "一个有信心的自我的确是心灵探险（psychic venturing）的先决条件，因为只有有自信的自我，才能最终让内我觉得足够安全，并留有回旋的余地。 [一个有自信的外我，是心灵旅程的前提。 只有自信的外我，才会有足够的安全感，在长线上让内我自由发挥。 外我与环境之间的牢固关系，应该视作认真深入探索心灵的必要前提。外我必须有回归之处。 自律不仅指内我对身体的精神约束，还包含内我对外我的训练约束，以使外我作为一个人格达成与物质宇宙的平衡关系。 如果没有这种自律， 内我的旅程就缺乏安全感，无可归处。真实平衡的心灵旅程，会为外我以及它处理事务的能力带来好处。 假若心灵旅程或探索令外我对环境失去掌控，这个人应当立刻暂停、提问。假如心灵探索以恰当的方式开始、假如外我与物质环境以恰当的方式关联，心灵探索将会提升外我的自我掌控能力。 ]", "en": "A confident ego is indeed a prerequisite for psychic venturing, for it is only the confident ego which ultimately feels secure enough to give leeway to the inner self in the long run.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第90节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "90", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0086", "zh": "很明显的，所谓的灵体投射常常在睡眠中发生。然而它也会在醒时发生，虽然自我通常并不觉知这样的投射。当通过练习，内我和外我之间会有更多的沟通，自我才更有机会明白，发生了什么。", "en": "Obviously then so-called astral projection occurs frequently in the sleeping state. It also occurs however in the waking state, although the ego is not aware of such projection as a rule. When through training there is greater communication between the inner and outer selves, then it is possible for the ego to realize what has happened.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第202节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "202", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0090", "zh": "当然，它某种程度上必定是成功的，不然你所知的物质导向人格就不存在了。自我当然是行动的一部分。然而，行动有无穷无尽的层面是自我感知不到的。内在自我和外在自我是可能融合到某种程度，而且这种融合在发生时的确代表一种新意识的形成。", "en": "It must, of course, succeed to some extent, or the physically oriented personality as you know it would not exist. The ego is of course a part of action. There are endless levels of action however, which the ego does not perceive. It is possible for the inner and outer egos to merge to some extent, and this merging when it occurs does indeed represent the formation of a new kind of consciousness.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第283节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "283", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0091", "zh": "这个观念算不上是新观念。它不是一般公认的理论，但它却源远流长。当你带着醒时的我(waking I）进入梦状态，这就是通往此一不同意识的途经。还有一个门户可能出现在醒时状况中。当这个门户开启时，内在自我和外在自我就会融合。外在自我认得它自己的职责，但它也觉察到还有更多东西牵涉在内。", "en": "This concept is hardly a new one. It is not a generally accepted theory, but it has ancient roots. When you carry the waking I into the dream state, this is one approach to this different consciousness. There is also an opening up that can occur in the waking condition. When this occurs the inner and outer egos merge. The outer ego recognizes its own duties, but it is aware that more is involved.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第283节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "283", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0092", "zh": "外在自我感应到它通常不得其门而入的实相。它想：“还有更多，但是我无法跟过去。”这里，有了这个了悟之后，内在自我可能会突然开启。直觉泉源冲到表面，因为外在自我已经改变了，它能够接受这些实相，同时依然履行它平常的职责。", "en": "It senses realities usually closed to it. It thinks, “There is more, but beyond I cannot follow.” Here with this realization the inner ego may suddenly open. Intuitive springs rush to the surface, and because the outer ego has already been alerted, it is able to accept these realities while still performing its ordinary duties.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第283节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "283", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0093", "zh": "然后可以取得的知识首先是创造、直觉的知识，如果可能，外在自我就会翻译成理智层面的说法。但它再也不怕直觉资料。它再也不抗拒内在感官，也不再恐惧它自己在直觉洪流之中的存活。", "en": "The knowledge then available is first of all creative, intuitive knowledge which the outer ego may translate into intellectual terms when possible. But it is no longer fearful of intuitive data. It no longer fights the inner senses, nor does it fear for its own survival in the midst of intuitional onrushes.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第283节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "283", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0094", "zh": "本体再也不受限于只有外在自我了。外在自我现在熟悉全我或整个本体，拥有它之前没有觉察到的力量可以取用。在朝气蓬勃的时期，你做事顺利，你的健康非比寻常地好，你能够记得并且操纵你的梦，所以这样的时期是这种意识出现的征兆。", "en": "Identity is no longer limited to the outer ego alone. The outer ego is now familiar with the whole self, or the entire identity, and has available to it strength of which it was not previously aware. In periods of exuberance, when you are working well, and your health is extraordinarily good, when you are able to remember and manipulate your dreams, then such periods are signs of the emergence of this new consciousness.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第283节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "283", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0095", "zh": "需要的发展很多都发生在梦状态中。约瑟，我想要提一下你在你家的后窗看到你自己的那一个梦。内在自我和外在自我融合了。受到惊吓的外在自我确实拦住你，不让你有一次绝佳的投射。", "en": "Much of the needed development takes place in the dream state. I wanted to mention that particular dream of yours, Joseph, in which you saw yourself at your back window. There was a merging of inner and outer egos. The startled outer ego did indeed hold you back from an excellent projection.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第283节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "283", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "外我从哪来、死后去哪：它不是用完就丢的工具", "note": "AI总结：外我有个出身故事：意识的中心——外向意识的中心——是内我在自己某些部分展现出更大的客观化倾向之后，最终选出来的；这些部分绕着某个潜意识次人格集结，胜出后成为外我，担任全我的操纵者和发言人。而它的结局更出人意料。内我确实是持久的自己，但各个外我极其重要，没有它们内我会被挡住、内在能力无从实现。一次特定的存在之后，外我并没有被吞噬：它继续掌控和指挥它聚焦过的那些力量，还能按照它与生俱来的能力、按照它与基本内我沟通的能力，在那个存在之后继续成长发展。当一个内我送出新的外我去进行新的冒险，先前的外我仍有几近无限的发展途径。如果内我与外我之间沟通良好，自我就会开始了解它是什么，认识到自己有比单一层面转世所能实现的更大的能力。有的外我满足于在同一个层面无限转世；有的则选择成为它们自己的存有——那个了不起的外我进而变成一个内在自我，再从它自己未实现的欲望和能力形成许多新的外我。但一个外我要走到这一步有条件：理解必须达到一定的程度。死亡之后，外我不再秀出它外在的那张脸，而是以人格的其他面向取而代之——你可以说它变成了潜意识，虽然这只是为了把概念讲清楚。", "src": "第 58、119、270 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 58 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 119 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 270 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-007-e0038", "zh": "这是真的，总之内我就是持久的自己（durable self）。虽然如此，各个不同的外在自我也极为重要，没有它们，内我就会被挡住。这些内在能力通常也无从实现。这么说吧，在一次特定的存在之后，外在自我不仅没有被吞噬，反而继续掌控它们在其形成与训练之时地位如此重要的那些特质与能力。", "en": "It is true that the inner self in the last analysis is the durable self. Nevertheless the various outer egos are extremely important, and without them the inner self would be blocked. Nor are these inner abilities as a rule ever left unfulfilled. The outer egos are not gobbled up, so to speak, after a particular existence, but remain in control of those characteristics and abilities which they have been so important in forming and training.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0039", "zh": "于是，外在自我最后仍然继续掌控和指挥那些它在某一个存在当中聚焦的力量。但甚至这也不是结束。它，也就是外在自我，根据它与生俱来的能力，并根据它与基本内我沟通的能力，甚至在那一特定的存在之后，还能够持续成长和发展。", "en": "The outer ego then remains at the end a controller and director of those strengths which it gathered about itself during its particular existence. But even this is not the end. It, that is it meaning the outer ego, can even continue growth and development after a particular existence, according to its inherent ability and according to its ability to communicate with the basic inner self.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0040", "zh": "我可以想像，这非常难以理解。但是，即使当一个内我送出了一个新的外在自我去进行一个新的伪装冒险，先前的自我还是有几近无限的发展途径。它有很多可能性。它可以选择保持现况，一个自我。然后留在一个有点附属于内我的位置上，但一点都不比它以前的附属地位低。", "en": "This is extremely difficult, I should imagine. Nevertheless, even when an inner self has sent out a new outer ego upon a new camouflage venture, the previous ego is still afforded an almost unlimited avenue for development. There are many possibilities for it. It can choose to remain what it is, one ego. It will then remain in a somewhat subordinate position to the inner self, but in no more of a subordinate position than it was earlier.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0041", "zh": "如果在自己，也就是内我和外在自我之间，有良好的沟通，那么自我就会开始了解它是什么，也会开始认识到它拥有的能力比它在单一层面持续转世所能实现的还要大。", "en": "Now if there is good communication between the self, that is the inner self and the outer ego, then the ego begins to understand what it is, and also to realize that it has greater capacities than it can realize by continued reincarnations, upon one plane.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0042", "zh": "其他的自我反而选择成为它们自己的存有，在这种例子里，那了不起的自我进而变为一个内在自我，然后从它自己未实现的欲望、能力和行动，形成许多新的外在自我，再度寻求价值完成。", "en": "Other egos choose instead to become entities of their own, in which case this magnificent outer ego becomes in turn an inner ego, which then from its own unfulfilled desires, abilities and initiatives are formed new outer egos which once again seek fulfillment.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0046", "zh": "你们记得，在你们层面或其他层面，都一定要符合某些必须的条件。可是，一个自我，一个外在自我，除非达到一定程度的理解，否则怎么样都无法选择成为一个存有。现在，我亲爱的、有耐心的约瑟，我可以告诉你，你也是那同一个存有的一部分；而我之所以能够和你们两位沟通，这就是主要原因之一。", "en": "There are certain requirements as you remember that must be met, upon your plane and upon others. Yet an ego, an outer ego, cannot choose to be an entity in any case until its comprehension attains a certain degree. And now, my dear patient Joseph, may I tell you also that you are part of that same entity; and this is one of the main reasons why I am able to communicate with you both.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0065", "zh": "意识的中心，也就是外向意识（outward consciousness）的中心，外在自我，在内我的某些部分展现更大的客观化倾向之后，最终被内在自我选上；这些部分当然绕着潜意识次人格的其中之一集结，然后胜出，成为外在自我，担任全我的操纵者和发言人。", "en": "The center of consciousness, that is the center of outward consciousness, the outer ego, is finally chosen by the inner ego after certain portions of the inner self show greater tendencies for objectification; these portions of course grouped around one of the subconscious subpersonalities which then wins out to become the outer ego, the manipulator for and the spokesman for the whole self.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第119节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "119", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0089", "zh": "死后犹存的人格有一种不同的心理平衡。外在自我不再秀出，可以说，它外在的那张脸（珍再次敲击桌面），而是以人格的其他面向取而代之。你可以说它变成潜意识，不过，我现在这样讲只是想把这个概念解释清楚而已，事实并不完全是如此。", "en": "The surviving personality has a different psychological balance. The outer ego no longer shows its outside face, so to speak, （again Jane struck the tabletop） but takes its place with the other aspects of the personality. You might say that ]t becomes the subconscious, although I am speaking now simply to get the idea across, and this is not precisely the case.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第270节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "270", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B08", "title": "别把头埋进沙子：松开对外我的过度认同", "note": "AI总结：这一块是赛斯给普通读者的提醒。你远比自我本位的「我是」大多了——你真正的人格包含一个更大、更有力量的内我；想通了这一点，外我拿不到内在知识这件事就不再困扰你。外我的理智只不过是内我一个黯淡的形象；潜意识最上层那点个人资料，职责本来就是维持意识自我的独裁掌控，它的抑制向来是为了保护自我。最有画面感的比方：没有镜子，眼睛看不到自己的瞳孔——外我在观看物质宇宙时，其实一直在跟自己内在自我的脸打照面，它逃不掉这个内我。你可以单单与外我认同、切断那些本是你一部的能力，可以否认，但改变不了事实——人格是多次元的，许多人却把头埋进三次元存在的沙里，假装没有更多的次元。赛斯开的方子很温柔：让外我觉知到组成它存在的无限力量，它就能放松、放下，感觉生命被支撑、安全，知道自己是宇宙所挚爱的孩子，既古老又年轻；外我越把「内在自我从宇宙性意识汲取即刻而持续的支持」这件事记在心里，它自己的稳定、安全与自尊感就越强。", "src": "第 3、49、54、87、119、434、512 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 3 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 49 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 54 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 87 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 119 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 434 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 512 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-007-e0027", "zh": "当你们了悟到你们远比自我本位的“我是”大多了，也明白你们真正的人格包含一个更大、更有力量的内我时，这种外在自我相对无法取得那份知识的状况，将不会再困扰你们。", "en": "When you realize that you are much more than the egotistical “I am,” and that your true personality contains a much larger and really more powerful inner ego, then this relative inavailability of inner comprehension to the outer ego will not annoy you.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第50节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "50", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0028", "zh": "于是，透过内在感官，你们可以感知内在法则，而且记得内在自我知道它是怎么一回事。外在自我的理智只不过是你们自己内在自我一个黯淡的形象。我们以后也会谈这一点。", "en": "Through the inner senses then, you may perceive the inner laws, and remember that the inner ego knows what it is about. The intellect of the outer ego is but a pale image of your own inner ego. We will also go into this later.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第54节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "54", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0049", "zh": "这里有一点：潜意识的上层或个人层与维持意识自我的独裁掌控和地位有关联。它的抑制向来的用意都是要保护自我。 [潜意识的最上层、个人层面，负责维持意识自我的专制控制和地位，它的抑制常常是为了保护外在自我。]", "en": "A point here: It is not understood at all that the uppermost or personal layer of the subconscious is concerned with maintaining the autocratic control and position of the conscious ego. Its inhibitions always are intended to protect the ego.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第87节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "87", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0062", "zh": "当外在自我，从它意识的表面，反映外在世界时，它看见内在自我的倒影，它们是在它自己眼睛之内的影像；就像自己在它自己的眼睛之内潜意识地创造物质，就像自己在潜意识里而不是在意识里创造物质，就像自己按照内在而不是外在的预期创造物质，同样的，自我也是，在观看物质宇宙时，与它自己内在自我的脸打照面；外在自我无法逃离这个内我。", "en": "When the outer ego, from the surface of its consciousness, reflects the outer world, it sees reflections of the inner ego which are the images within its own eye; and as the self creates matter subconsciously within its own eye, and as the self creates matter subconsciously and not consciously, and as the self creates matter in line with inner and not outer expectations, so then does the ego, in viewing the material universe, come face to face with the face of its own inner ego; and the outer ego cannot escape from this inner self.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第119节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "119", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0099", "zh": "有一个讨人喜欢的外我，它对着遇见的人微笑，和善地点头，打着旋儿、欢跳着。然而在底下，却对这样一个外我怀着恐惧。就你们现在的此刻而言，内我还没有找到、也还没有聚焦它真正的才能或方向，所以它惧怕自己、回避自己，因而常常怨恨外我的能量。", "en": "There is a delightful outer self, and it smiles and nods genially at those it meets, and pirouettes and prances. Underneath however there is a fear of this outer self. The inner self, in your present, has not yet found nor focused its true ability or direction, and so it fears itself avoid and therefore often resents the energy of the outer self.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第434节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "434", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0107", "zh": "为了方便起见，你把那些跳过你肉体最细微部分之间的多方面的内在沟通关在外面，但即使当你是有肉体的生物时，你在某一个程度仍是其他意识的一部分。“自己”是无限的，它的潜能也是无限的。然而，因为你自己的无知你可能会采取人为的限制。例如，你能单单与你的外面自我认同，而与本是你一部的那些能力切断。你可以否认事实，却无法改变它。拿驼鸟作个比喻，虽然许多人将他们的头埋在三次元存在的沙中，而假装没有更多的次元，但是人格的确是多次元的。", "en": "For convenience’s sake, you close out the multitudinous inner communications that leap between the tiniest parts of your flesh, yet even as physical creatures, you are to some extent a portion of other consciousnesses. There are no limitations to the self. There are no limitations to its potentials. (Pause.) You can adopt artificial limitations through your own ignorance, however. You can identify, for example, with your outer ego alone, and cut yourself off from abilities that are a part of you. You can deny, but you cannot change, the facts. The personality is multidimensional, even though many people hide their heads, figuratively speaking, in the sand of three-dimensional existence and pretend there is nothing more.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第512节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "512", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0117", "zh": "它也觉察组成它存在的布料本身之无限力量与力气。借由使得外在自我觉察到这些事实，它也能开始感觉一种加快的支持与滋润感。那知识能让它放松、放下，因此它感觉其生命被支撑与安全，而知道自己的确是宇宙之一个被挚爱的孩子，同时既古老又年轻，有着一个远超过时间历史的身份。", "en": "(Pause at 4:33.) It is also aware of the infinite power and strength that composes the very fabric of its being. Through being made aware of these facts, the exterior ego can begin to feel a quicker sense of support and nourishment. The knowledge can let it relax, let go, so that it feels its life couched and safe, and knows itself to be indeed a beloved child of the universe, both ancient and young at once, with an identity far beyond the annals of time.", "source": "健康之道 · 第3节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "3", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-007-e0118", "zh": "那么，每一个人都记住这宇宙性的联盟，是极其重要的。这样的一个提醒，往往容许内在自我经由种种不同的层面，送出力量和爱的必要信息，显示为灵感、梦，或单纯的情感爆岭。内在自我（停顿良久）从宇宙性的意识汲取即刻而持续的支持，而外在自我越将这事实谨记在心，它自己的稳定、安全与自尊感越强。", "en": "It is of great value, then, that each person remember this universal affiliation. Such a reminder can often allow the inner self to send needed messages of strength and love through the various levels, appearing as inspiration, dreams, or simply pure bursts of feeling. The inner ego (long pause) draws instant and continuous support from the universal consciousness, and the more the exterior ego keeps that fact in mind, the greater its own sense of stability, safety, and self-esteem.", "source": "健康之道 · 第3节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "3", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [], "books": [{"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 16}, {"name": "早期课第2册", "count": 16}, {"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 10}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 8}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 6}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第5册", "count": 2}, {"name": "个人与群体事件的本质", "count": 2}, {"name": "健康之道", "count": 2}, {"name": "时空之外", "count": 1}, {"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 1}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 1}, {"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 1}], "span": [1963, 1984], "stats": {"blocks": 8, "quotes": 71, "reading": 0, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 0, "only_en": 2}};
